1
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:26,480
I’m a new person now.

2
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:28,220
I apologize for what I did in the past.

3
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,570
Why are we secretly following Lord Gaew?

4
00:01:32,570 --> 00:01:34,420
I’m afraid he’s going to cause trouble.

5
00:01:37,620 --> 00:01:39,580
You can call me Falcon.

6
00:01:43,860 --> 00:01:45,150
What’s happening to me?

7
00:01:45,470 --> 00:01:47,900
Why is my heart racing like this?

8
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:50,460
Lord Muen.

9
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:53,220
Muen Reung Ratchaphakdi has arrived with the police.

10
00:01:57,009 --> 00:01:58,530
Oh my, Muen Reung!

11
00:01:59,990 --> 00:02:01,110
Why are you arresting me?

12
00:02:02,950 --> 00:02:04,740
What happened, Muen Reung?

13
00:02:05,710 --> 00:02:08,220
Gaew is the prime suspect in a murder case.

14
00:02:08,410 --> 00:02:09,729
Murder?

15
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:11,890
Me? A murderer?

16
00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:13,820
Calm down, Reung.

17
00:02:14,140 --> 00:02:15,820
This must be a misunderstanding.

18
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:18,920
But my master, Khun Ratchapinit,

19
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:22,550
received information that Gaew did it,

20
00:02:24,650 --> 00:02:25,420
Take him away.

21
00:02:26,570 --> 00:02:27,320
My lord.

22
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:28,630
My lord!

23
00:02:28,950 --> 00:02:30,740
Why are you arresting me? Let me go!

24
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:32,090
I didn’t kill anyone!

25
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:43,130
What happened?

26
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:45,510
There was a murder last night.

27
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:49,490
Who was the victim?

28
00:02:50,270 --> 00:02:52,780
Dam, a poet at the pier.

29
00:02:53,290 --> 00:02:54,780
His body was found behind the market.

30
00:02:56,810 --> 00:02:57,670
Falcon!

31
00:02:58,329 --> 00:02:59,800
Falcon, please help me!

32
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:00,630
Falcon!

33
00:03:01,470 --> 00:03:03,260
Please, please help me!

34
00:03:06,430 --> 00:03:08,690
I swear I didn’t kill the thief last night.

35
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:10,100
I didn’t kill him.

36
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:11,940
Please testify that I’m innocent.

37
00:03:12,140 --> 00:03:13,780
Please, help me.

38
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:14,940
Please.

39
00:03:15,190 --> 00:03:15,990
Falcon.

40
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:17,180
Please.

41
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:19,210
You can speak a foreign language?

42
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:36,350
No.

43
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:38,500
I picked it up here and there.

44
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:49,670
Then I’ll take him to the police department.

45
00:03:51,770 --> 00:03:52,620
Falcon.

46
00:04:00,020 --> 00:04:00,710
Let’s go.

47
00:04:03,490 --> 00:04:05,340
Please. Please!

48
00:04:05,340 --> 00:04:06,470
-I didn’t kill him.
-My lord!

49
00:04:06,470 --> 00:04:07,590
Please help me.

50
00:04:09,510 --> 00:04:11,910
P’Muen, please help me.

51
00:04:13,940 --> 00:04:15,180
You two go home first.

52
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:17,130
I’ll take care of this.

53
00:04:17,380 --> 00:04:18,329
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

54
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:22,560
Please help me, P’Muen!

55
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:25,380
I didn’t do it!

56
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:13,180
Gaew.

57
00:05:13,690 --> 00:05:14,780
Just confess.

58
00:05:15,270 --> 00:05:16,560
Your punishment will be lighter.

59
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:19,990
Confess to what? I didn’t do it, Reung.

60
00:05:22,550 --> 00:05:23,690
If you didn’t,

61
00:05:24,390 --> 00:05:25,910
then how did Dam die?

62
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:28,370
I don’t know.

63
00:05:28,630 --> 00:05:31,290
He didn’t die because of me.

64
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:33,260
I didn’t kill him. Let me go!

65
00:05:35,070 --> 00:05:36,460
If you don’t know,

66
00:05:36,900 --> 00:05:38,210
then who does?

67
00:05:38,630 --> 00:05:40,950
I don’t know. Let me go!

68
00:05:40,950 --> 00:05:42,300
I didn’t do it!

69
00:05:44,070 --> 00:05:45,470
If you don’t confess,

70
00:05:46,250 --> 00:05:47,470
we’ll whip you until you do!

71
00:05:47,820 --> 00:05:48,520
Yes, sir.

72
00:06:18,750 --> 00:06:19,860
Ten of Swords.

73
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:22,990
Be careful of being falsely accused.

74
00:06:27,660 --> 00:06:30,140
And this one is pretty serious.

75
00:06:32,030 --> 00:06:33,560
Serious enough to draw blood.

76
00:06:46,450 --> 00:06:48,659
You’ll feel like fate is playing a cruel joke on you,

77
00:06:48,860 --> 00:06:50,700
but it’s an old karma that can’t be avoided.

78
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:53,060
Your enemy may not want your life,

79
00:06:53,610 --> 00:06:56,140
but they do want you destroyed.

80
00:06:56,790 --> 00:06:58,280
You must be good,

81
00:06:58,580 --> 00:07:00,250
be patient,

82
00:07:00,410 --> 00:07:01,950
and you’ll make it through.

83
00:07:14,580 --> 00:07:15,430
P’Muen?

84
00:07:16,370 --> 00:07:17,080
Gaew.

85
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:18,280
P’Muen!

86
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:19,010
Gaew.

87
00:07:21,410 --> 00:07:22,180
P’Muen.

88
00:07:22,710 --> 00:07:24,130
I didn’t kill anyone!

89
00:07:24,730 --> 00:07:25,710
You saw it.

90
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:27,870
I fought with my bare hands.

91
00:07:28,510 --> 00:07:29,570
The man who died…

92
00:07:30,420 --> 00:07:31,620
was stabbed.

93
00:07:31,620 --> 00:07:32,930
It really wasn’t me.

94
00:07:34,409 --> 00:07:35,540
I believe you, Gaew.

95
00:07:37,990 --> 00:07:38,909
Sir.

96
00:07:39,790 --> 00:07:42,340
I can testify for Gaew.

97
00:07:42,909 --> 00:07:43,830
How so, Dech?

98
00:08:21,590 --> 00:08:24,140
Dam didn’t die during the fight

99
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:25,890
at Mali’s shop, did he?

100
00:08:27,710 --> 00:08:28,530
No.

101
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:31,630
Then where was the body found?

102
00:08:32,210 --> 00:08:34,190
Behind the market during the second night watch.

103
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:37,450
A witness saw Dam being stabbed.

104
00:08:40,100 --> 00:08:41,110
At that time,

105
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:44,120
Gaew was with me at the house.

106
00:08:48,540 --> 00:08:50,940
And he was completely drunk.

107
00:08:53,870 --> 00:08:56,660
Then who did it?

108
00:09:20,290 --> 00:09:23,360
I can testify that Gaew didn’t do it.

109
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:39,370
Release him.

110
00:09:41,060 --> 00:09:43,420
He’s not the culprit.

111
00:09:44,770 --> 00:09:45,470
Release him?

112
00:09:47,020 --> 00:09:49,110
Even though he killed Dam

113
00:09:50,060 --> 00:09:51,940
and still refuses to admit it?

114
00:09:52,370 --> 00:09:53,550
Think about it.

115
00:09:54,290 --> 00:09:55,640
Dam was a notorious thief

116
00:09:56,520 --> 00:09:59,300
who was already wanted.

117
00:10:01,890 --> 00:10:04,040
Now that he’s dead, the villagers can finally rest easy.

118
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:05,970
That’s true.

119
00:10:06,520 --> 00:10:08,620
Dam was a thief.

120
00:10:09,820 --> 00:10:11,270
But Gaew also committed a crime.

121
00:10:11,710 --> 00:10:12,620
He killed someone.

122
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:14,600
Do you have any evidence

123
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:16,990
that Gaew killed him?

124
00:10:19,730 --> 00:10:21,270
Someone saw Gaew

125
00:10:21,930 --> 00:10:23,620
fighting with Dam.

126
00:10:27,380 --> 00:10:29,090
But no one saw

127
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:32,340
Gaew stab him.

128
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:33,830
Isn’t that right?

129
00:10:38,460 --> 00:10:39,260
Yes.

130
00:10:40,030 --> 00:10:41,580
We only found the body.

131
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:45,000
Release him, then.

132
00:10:47,190 --> 00:10:50,620
You can’t arrest an innocent person.

133
00:10:51,570 --> 00:10:54,270
Why are you so sure?

134
00:10:55,350 --> 00:10:56,930
If it wasn’t Gaew,

135
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:59,930
then who killed Dam?

136
00:12:22,970 --> 00:12:24,310
I did.

137
00:12:32,470 --> 00:12:33,340
Your Honor.

138
00:12:34,050 --> 00:12:35,270
I'm a witness.

139
00:12:55,590 --> 00:12:58,110
He had no choice but to fight back

140
00:12:58,500 --> 00:12:59,790
to protect himself

141
00:13:01,430 --> 00:13:02,380
and to save me.

142
00:13:04,130 --> 00:13:05,010
Otherwise,

143
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:06,870
the body you found

144
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:08,970
wouldn’t have been that thief’s.

145
00:13:09,900 --> 00:13:11,140
It would’ve been mine

146
00:13:13,050 --> 00:13:14,410
and His Lordship’s.

147
00:13:51,100 --> 00:13:52,830
I can’t accept your generosity.

148
00:13:57,650 --> 00:13:58,510
Then…

149
00:14:00,660 --> 00:14:03,430
are you going to punish an innocent man?

150
00:14:08,990 --> 00:14:09,740
Yes, sir.

151
00:14:20,890 --> 00:14:21,820
Okkhun.

152
00:14:22,730 --> 00:14:24,380
You didn’t neglect your duty.

153
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:27,290
You simply can’t charge me,

154
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:29,590
a man who fights back in self defense

155
00:14:30,790 --> 00:14:33,160
and accidentally kills Dam…

156
00:14:34,330 --> 00:14:37,290
Without any evidence, you can’t charge Gaew either.

157
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:41,090
Releasing him

158
00:14:42,170 --> 00:14:44,140
is the right thing to do,

159
00:14:44,950 --> 00:14:45,950
isn’t it?

160
00:15:39,820 --> 00:15:41,980
Gaew’s name has been cleared, Dech.

161
00:15:44,510 --> 00:15:45,910
I’m sorry, Gaew.

162
00:15:46,630 --> 00:15:49,000
It was my duty.

163
00:15:54,290 --> 00:15:58,660
How did you convince him that Gaew is innocent?

164
00:16:02,540 --> 00:16:05,260
I only did what was right.

165
00:16:07,350 --> 00:16:08,570
It’s only natural.

166
00:16:15,910 --> 00:16:17,550
Are you heading home, Maria?

167
00:16:18,850 --> 00:16:19,780
I’ll walk you home.

168
00:16:24,450 --> 00:16:25,300
Alright.

169
00:16:38,010 --> 00:16:39,220
Let’s go home, Gaew.

170
00:17:19,160 --> 00:17:19,980
Wad.

171
00:17:21,980 --> 00:17:23,980
Reung, are you done with work?

172
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:25,700
Why are you here?

173
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:27,490
Yes.

174
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:29,740
Go wait at the boat.

175
00:17:30,740 --> 00:17:31,470
Yes, sir.

176
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:38,040
You look exhausted.

177
00:17:39,590 --> 00:17:42,410
I just finished presiding over Gaew’s case.

178
00:17:43,730 --> 00:17:45,080
I was just about to ask.

179
00:17:45,780 --> 00:17:48,030
What was the verdict?

180
00:17:50,510 --> 00:17:52,120
No matter how much they tortured him,

181
00:17:52,810 --> 00:17:54,450
Gaew still wouldn’t confess.

182
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:56,550
That’s not surprising.

183
00:17:57,310 --> 00:18:00,390
He’s never admitted to any wrongdoing.

184
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:03,180
But after being tortured like that,

185
00:18:04,220 --> 00:18:07,530
he’d eventually confess.

186
00:18:08,670 --> 00:18:09,560
That’s not it.

187
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:12,450
Gaew has already been released.

188
00:18:14,900 --> 00:18:16,180
How did that happen?

189
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:18,860
I’d like to know too.

190
00:18:19,820 --> 00:18:21,750
But it was Okkhun’s order,

191
00:18:22,760 --> 00:18:25,310
so I couldn’t question his decision.

192
00:18:30,620 --> 00:18:32,060
Still, I’m quite relieved.

193
00:18:34,090 --> 00:18:38,060
Dech was so worried about Gaew.

194
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:40,610
As soon as Gaew was released,

195
00:18:40,610 --> 00:18:42,640
he personally took him home.

196
00:18:47,260 --> 00:18:51,020
Now he’s probably busy taking care of him.

197
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:06,770
My lady, they’re back.

198
00:19:18,470 --> 00:19:19,350
Pin, Yam.

199
00:19:20,110 --> 00:19:21,500
Take Gaew to his room.

200
00:19:21,660 --> 00:19:22,510
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

201
00:19:28,420 --> 00:19:29,110
Dech.

202
00:19:30,710 --> 00:19:31,700
Talk to me first.

203
00:19:33,010 --> 00:19:35,310
How did Gaew make it out of this?

204
00:19:38,310 --> 00:19:41,670
Lord Luang Surasakorn talked to Okkhun Ratchaphinit.

205
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:44,410
He testified that Gaew was innocent.

206
00:19:45,190 --> 00:19:47,430
How could it be so easy?

207
00:19:48,690 --> 00:19:50,890
Get more out of him, P’Hora.

208
00:19:54,100 --> 00:19:55,480
I have no more questions.

209
00:19:55,950 --> 00:19:57,720
Let’s stop pestering him, Jumpa.

210
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:01,210
Just know that...

211
00:20:02,510 --> 00:20:03,580
Gaew’s name has been cleared.

212
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:10,850
Is there anything else?

213
00:20:11,620 --> 00:20:13,660
I’ll go check on Gaew.

214
00:20:18,110 --> 00:20:20,230
Juang, go get the herbs.

215
00:20:20,230 --> 00:20:21,510
Then follow me.

216
00:20:21,510 --> 00:20:22,280
Yes, sir.

217
00:20:29,090 --> 00:20:30,220
Prepare the medicine for me.

218
00:20:30,220 --> 00:20:31,130
Yes, my lord.

219
00:20:50,460 --> 00:20:51,780
Is that Kanom Kong?

220
00:20:52,510 --> 00:20:53,250
Yes.

221
00:20:57,300 --> 00:20:58,300
I’ll take two pieces.

222
00:21:04,010 --> 00:21:04,760
Here you go.

223
00:21:25,890 --> 00:21:26,760
Eat some.

224
00:21:27,430 --> 00:21:28,420
It’ll cheer you up.

225
00:21:29,900 --> 00:21:31,130
I’m not in a bad mood.

226
00:21:34,780 --> 00:21:36,250
If you won’t eat it, then I will.

227
00:21:51,410 --> 00:21:52,890
I’ve been curious for a while.

228
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:55,590
Why do you like Kanom Kong so much?

229
00:21:56,490 --> 00:21:57,780
You’ve been eating it since childhood.

230
00:21:59,670 --> 00:22:00,910
You still remember?

231
00:22:07,270 --> 00:22:08,740
It tastes great

232
00:22:09,980 --> 00:22:11,400
and has a beautiful meaning.

233
00:22:13,810 --> 00:22:16,020
I understand it tastes good.

234
00:22:17,640 --> 00:22:21,640
But what does its meaning have to do with that?

235
00:22:22,250 --> 00:22:23,670
So what’s the meaning?

236
00:22:28,340 --> 00:22:29,240
Kanom Kong.

237
00:22:31,900 --> 00:22:34,390
It symbolizes an unwavering love.

238
00:22:39,160 --> 00:22:42,050
An unwavering love?

239
00:22:44,710 --> 00:22:46,060
An unwavering love.

240
00:22:52,660 --> 00:22:53,670
Where are you going?

241
00:22:54,910 --> 00:22:56,820
I’m going to buy Kanom Kong for Dech.

242
00:23:08,650 --> 00:23:09,640
Lord Muen.

243
00:23:10,420 --> 00:23:11,400
It’s done.

244
00:23:19,090 --> 00:23:21,070
Was Wad here to get some herbs?

245
00:23:21,070 --> 00:23:21,880
Yes.

246
00:23:22,340 --> 00:23:24,220
Only agarwood is missing.

247
00:23:24,550 --> 00:23:25,700
It’s really hard to find.

248
00:23:27,480 --> 00:23:30,140
Agarwood?

249
00:23:55,220 --> 00:24:05,900
What is that mark upon your rosy cheeks?

250
00:24:06,490 --> 00:24:15,500
Did some insect dare to kiss you in your sleep?

251
00:24:23,150 --> 00:24:27,660
Skin so fair, no hand would dare to touch.

252
00:24:30,130 --> 00:24:36,420
Such flawless grace that should be embraced,

253
00:24:42,140 --> 00:24:42,860
Excellent.

254
00:24:44,210 --> 00:24:48,030
It looks like I’ll finally have a royal court poet.

255
00:24:49,180 --> 00:24:51,330
From now on, if I’m stuck writing a poem,

256
00:24:51,840 --> 00:24:53,440
I’ll have a royal poet to help me.

257
00:24:55,300 --> 00:24:56,080
Sri.

258
00:24:57,630 --> 00:24:58,410
Come here.

259
00:25:45,760 --> 00:25:46,960
This ring…

260
00:25:47,780 --> 00:25:50,550
I’m giving it to you as a symbol

261
00:25:51,300 --> 00:25:53,420
that you are my greatest poet.

262
00:25:59,010 --> 00:26:02,850
I hereby appoint you as Phra Sriprach.

263
00:26:45,460 --> 00:26:48,700
I am deeply honored by Your Majesty’s boundless grace.

264
00:26:49,430 --> 00:26:51,020
Hahaha.

265
00:26:51,810 --> 00:26:52,770
Okya.

266
00:26:53,850 --> 00:26:54,660
Yes, your majesty.

267
00:26:55,610 --> 00:26:58,800
Your son will be appointed as Phra Sriprach.

268
00:26:59,710 --> 00:27:02,330
Thank you for your kindness.

269
00:27:03,700 --> 00:27:05,420
Word has spread throughout the palace

270
00:27:06,070 --> 00:27:09,300
that your family is blessed with talented sons.

271
00:27:09,820 --> 00:27:10,750
There’s Sri,

272
00:27:11,170 --> 00:27:11,970
Dech,

273
00:27:12,370 --> 00:27:13,270
and another one,

274
00:27:13,870 --> 00:27:16,710
Gaew, who speaks foreign languages.

275
00:27:17,790 --> 00:27:21,660
You’ll have to bring him to serve me soon.

276
00:27:24,660 --> 00:27:25,530
Yes, Your Majesty.

277
00:27:50,470 --> 00:27:51,200
Lek.

278
00:27:52,390 --> 00:27:53,450
You’re here.

279
00:27:57,760 --> 00:27:58,570
Tia.

280
00:27:59,010 --> 00:27:59,790
Sri.

281
00:28:00,160 --> 00:28:01,020
You may leave.

282
00:28:03,940 --> 00:28:04,800
Yes, your majesty.

283
00:28:16,570 --> 00:28:19,410
I’ll ask you one last time.

284
00:28:21,280 --> 00:28:24,510
Are you still standing by the same answer?

285
00:28:33,760 --> 00:28:34,670
Answer me!

286
00:28:46,380 --> 00:28:47,340
Yes, your majesty!

287
00:29:44,170 --> 00:29:45,290
Wait for me at the boat.

288
00:29:45,650 --> 00:29:46,390
Yes, sir.

289
00:30:03,410 --> 00:30:04,690
Is the lotus not beautiful?

290
00:30:10,720 --> 00:30:14,150
Why does its owner sigh

291
00:30:14,690 --> 00:30:16,530
instead of admiring its beauty?

292
00:30:20,890 --> 00:30:23,210
I didn’t mean to startle you.

293
00:30:24,530 --> 00:30:25,760
I’m just passing by.

294
00:30:48,330 --> 00:30:51,520
If I wish to admire the lotus in your hand,

295
00:30:53,990 --> 00:30:56,580
would you allow me?

296
00:31:00,150 --> 00:31:01,490
Beautiful?

297
00:31:03,570 --> 00:31:07,500
Once it’s been plucked from the pond,

298
00:31:11,280 --> 00:31:13,330
there’s nothing left worth admiring.

299
00:31:17,910 --> 00:31:20,880
A lotus doesn’t lose its beauty just because it’s been picked,

300
00:31:23,150 --> 00:31:26,630
but the one who plucks it out must be careful.

301
00:31:27,890 --> 00:31:30,070
They must cradle it gently, so it won’t be bruised.

302
00:31:32,290 --> 00:31:34,820
Once a lotus has been picked,

303
00:31:41,280 --> 00:31:42,390
do you think

304
00:31:44,580 --> 00:31:46,850
it should be happy to be chosen,

305
00:31:48,010 --> 00:31:49,570
or saddened...

306
00:31:50,690 --> 00:31:53,680
because it never got to choose?

307
00:31:56,400 --> 00:31:57,660
The one that is chosen

308
00:31:58,660 --> 00:32:00,370
must be the most beautiful lotus.

309
00:32:01,250 --> 00:32:05,170
Otherwise, no one would’ve wanted it.

310
00:32:09,580 --> 00:32:10,950
So I believe

311
00:32:11,910 --> 00:32:14,020
that lotus is truly precious.

312
00:32:14,730 --> 00:32:16,240
And the one who gets to cherish it

313
00:32:17,180 --> 00:32:18,750
must be greatly blessed.

314
00:32:34,470 --> 00:32:36,540
A lotus bud waits beneath the water

315
00:32:39,010 --> 00:32:41,010
until it’s time to bloom.

316
00:32:43,500 --> 00:32:44,820
It can never know

317
00:32:45,810 --> 00:32:48,220
where fate will carry it.

318
00:33:07,920 --> 00:33:09,030
I’ll be going now.

319
00:33:29,280 --> 00:33:31,040
May I know your name?

320
00:33:34,820 --> 00:33:35,900
My name is…

321
00:33:38,390 --> 00:33:39,110
Jam.

322
00:33:54,310 --> 00:33:55,030
Jam.

323
00:34:13,070 --> 00:34:13,790
Gaew.

324
00:34:15,409 --> 00:34:16,590
How are you feeling?

325
00:34:18,520 --> 00:34:19,699
I’m alright.

326
00:34:21,330 --> 00:34:22,840
Oh, my lord.

327
00:34:25,100 --> 00:34:26,650
Let me take your shirt off.

328
00:34:28,150 --> 00:34:29,989
Yam, help me take it off.

329
00:34:29,989 --> 00:34:30,699
Yes, sir.

330
00:34:35,449 --> 00:34:36,139
Ow.

331
00:34:44,440 --> 00:34:45,389
Let me have a look.

332
00:34:57,330 --> 00:34:59,010
I’ll put some medicine on it.

333
00:35:04,930 --> 00:35:07,080
Pin, Yam, wait outside.

334
00:35:07,590 --> 00:35:08,350
Yes, sir.

335
00:35:31,050 --> 00:35:31,910
Easy.

336
00:35:48,920 --> 00:35:49,690
Ow.

337
00:35:55,550 --> 00:35:56,830
I’m sorry.

338
00:35:58,250 --> 00:35:59,830
I couldn’t help you.

339
00:36:03,650 --> 00:36:05,370
Just treating my wounds

340
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:07,870
is more than enough.

341
00:36:17,530 --> 00:36:18,300
Ow.

342
00:36:39,950 --> 00:36:40,910
Come on.

343
00:36:41,690 --> 00:36:43,180
Eat something, then take your medicine.

344
00:38:04,490 --> 00:38:05,450
That’s enough, P’Muen.

345
00:39:27,540 --> 00:39:30,980
You sleep so peacefully, no harm can come near.

346
00:39:34,310 --> 00:39:37,920
Close your eyes, there’s nothing left to fear.

347
00:39:42,430 --> 00:39:46,230
Rest your head upon my lap and let your worries fade away.

348
00:39:50,510 --> 00:39:54,210
I’ll guard you safely until the break of day.

349
00:40:01,460 --> 00:40:05,260
I wonder how you came to face such cruel misfortune.

350
00:40:07,630 --> 00:40:11,250
What kind of karma brought you to such ruin?

351
00:40:13,850 --> 00:40:17,700
If heaven grants one prayer to me,

352
00:40:19,940 --> 00:40:24,190
may you live a life that’s safe, forever free.

353
00:40:35,020 --> 00:40:36,230
Why do I…

354
00:40:37,470 --> 00:40:39,400
keep looking at you

355
00:40:40,120 --> 00:40:41,160
whether you’re asleep

356
00:40:42,230 --> 00:40:43,730
or awake?

357
00:40:48,420 --> 00:40:49,160
So,

358
00:40:50,070 --> 00:40:51,100
who is Gaew?

359
00:40:51,210 --> 00:40:51,850
Huh?

360
00:40:52,650 --> 00:40:54,040
You are Gaew.

361
00:40:55,430 --> 00:40:57,700
Have you really lost your memory?

362
00:41:22,050 --> 00:41:23,340
Will you even believe me?

363
00:41:23,340 --> 00:41:24,280
Just tell me!

364
00:41:27,490 --> 00:41:28,730
I want lightning to strike me,

365
00:41:29,290 --> 00:41:30,760
so I can go back to where I came from.

366
00:41:35,320 --> 00:41:36,770
Where I live…

367
00:41:41,410 --> 00:41:42,900
I mean the city I live in…

368
00:41:44,540 --> 00:41:45,880
has so much light,

369
00:41:47,080 --> 00:41:48,770
so we never see this many stars.

370
00:42:02,860 --> 00:42:03,710
Well?

371
00:42:10,410 --> 00:42:12,440
What’s the Krishna Kali spell, P’Muen?

372
00:42:13,210 --> 00:42:14,730
it’s a prayer chant.

373
00:42:15,890 --> 00:42:17,220
You weren’t feeling well before,

374
00:42:18,100 --> 00:42:19,260
so I prayed for you.

375
00:42:21,030 --> 00:42:22,590
What kind of prayer

376
00:42:23,780 --> 00:42:26,260
sends me across centuries?

377
00:42:28,090 --> 00:42:29,140
What did you say?

378
00:42:35,450 --> 00:42:40,660
The closer we get, the deeper it grows

379
00:42:42,060 --> 00:42:48,970
The deeper it grows, the clearer it shows

380
00:42:48,970 --> 00:42:54,410
Now I understand my own heart

381
00:42:54,410 --> 00:43:00,910
Without you, my life would fall apart

382
00:43:01,480 --> 00:43:08,260
Are you the one I’ve waited for so long?

383
00:43:08,260 --> 00:43:15,060
Never has my heart yearned quite this strong

384
00:43:15,060 --> 00:43:21,830
If heaven decreed that we are meant to be

385
00:43:21,830 --> 00:43:26,970
How could I deny the feelings inside of me?

386
00:43:26,970 --> 00:43:30,140
Oh, my beloved

387
00:43:31,560 --> 00:43:35,800
How’s Okya-Kosathibodi’s work going?

388
00:43:36,570 --> 00:43:39,020
He’s been very busy, Jumpa.

389
00:43:39,570 --> 00:43:42,200
It’d be nice to have someone lighten his workload.

390
00:43:43,690 --> 00:43:44,860
Did you know?

391
00:43:45,160 --> 00:43:48,760
Gaew, the son of Okya-Ramnarong and Pudjeeb,

392
00:43:48,760 --> 00:43:51,160
whom I took in and raised,

393
00:43:51,160 --> 00:43:54,760
speaks foreign languages fluently.

394
00:43:55,270 --> 00:43:56,620
Dech told me

395
00:43:56,900 --> 00:43:59,410
he naturally spoke with Lord Luang Surasakorn

396
00:43:59,410 --> 00:44:02,110
as if it were his native tongue.

397
00:44:02,450 --> 00:44:04,470
He’s truly impressive.

398
00:44:06,900 --> 00:44:07,730
Oh?

399
00:44:08,250 --> 00:44:10,190
But back then,

400
00:44:10,540 --> 00:44:13,240
didn’t you extremely despise him?

401
00:44:15,130 --> 00:44:16,780
And I also heard that

402
00:44:17,190 --> 00:44:20,270
you tried to kick him out several times.

403
00:44:21,090 --> 00:44:22,450
Goodness.

404
00:44:22,670 --> 00:44:24,010
she’s heard quite a lot.

405
00:44:25,960 --> 00:44:26,900
Right my lady?

406
00:44:30,300 --> 00:44:33,240
I’ve raised Gaew since he was a child.

407
00:44:33,510 --> 00:44:36,970
After all these years, he’s like my own son.

408
00:44:37,170 --> 00:44:39,750
I’ve taught him and scolded him,

409
00:44:39,750 --> 00:44:43,270
but no mother hates her child.

410
00:44:43,660 --> 00:44:45,060
You mostly scolded him, though.

411
00:44:45,810 --> 00:44:46,730
Prik!

412
00:44:51,860 --> 00:44:58,260
Gaew is so gifted with foreign languages.

413
00:44:58,260 --> 00:45:01,060
It would be wonderful if he could serve His Majesty

414
00:45:01,340 --> 00:45:05,660
and give something back to the kingdom.

415
00:45:06,310 --> 00:45:07,390
That’s true.

416
00:45:23,820 --> 00:45:25,330
I miss Grandma so much.

417
00:45:26,370 --> 00:45:28,070
Will she be alright?

418
00:45:33,150 --> 00:45:33,980
My lord.

419
00:45:37,530 --> 00:45:38,580
What is it, P’Yam?

420
00:45:43,380 --> 00:45:46,690
Here are rice porridge and medicine from Lady Jumpa.

421
00:45:48,070 --> 00:45:49,070
Really?

422
00:45:49,070 --> 00:45:51,990
Yes, she even cooked it herself.

423
00:46:34,250 --> 00:46:36,030
What do you think? Am I amazing?

424
00:46:36,030 --> 00:46:37,090
Who are you?

425
00:46:37,090 --> 00:46:38,860
You’re not my younger brother.

426
00:46:39,350 --> 00:46:40,470
Ah!

427
00:46:40,770 --> 00:46:41,550
My lord!

428
00:46:45,250 --> 00:46:47,770
I told you I'm a doctor.

429
00:46:48,930 --> 00:46:51,010
Read this poem.

430
00:46:51,010 --> 00:46:53,170
I could tell at a glance it was yours.

431
00:46:53,620 --> 00:46:55,180
Please forgive me.

432
00:46:55,700 --> 00:46:57,490
I didn’t know my place

433
00:46:58,430 --> 00:47:00,690
I wish I could bathe with you like this

434
00:47:00,690 --> 00:47:01,810
every day.

435
00:47:03,710 --> 00:47:04,830
Please slow down.

436
00:47:05,460 --> 00:47:06,330
Step back.

437
00:47:21,660 --> 00:47:24,620
Shall we make a heart?

438
00:47:25,250 --> 00:47:26,170
What are you doing?

439
00:47:26,170 --> 00:47:27,150
Taking a photo.

440
00:47:27,150 --> 00:47:27,790
Ah!

441
00:47:28,850 --> 00:47:29,840
Dr. Reungrich.

442
00:47:31,130 --> 00:47:34,920
This is Wayu, our new male nurse.

443
00:47:35,250 --> 00:47:36,970
He’s been here for less than a week.

444
00:47:37,660 --> 00:47:40,060
Isn’t he so handsome?

445
00:47:41,710 --> 00:47:43,830
He’s by far the most handsome.

446
00:47:44,140 --> 00:47:45,900
He’s only been here for a few days,

447
00:47:45,900 --> 00:47:50,330
and already won over all the patients and nurses.

448
00:47:50,960 --> 00:47:54,460
He’s so charming, Doctor.

449
00:47:54,720 --> 00:47:55,930
You think this is handsome?

450
00:48:03,530 --> 00:48:04,860
He looks like a lizard.

451
00:48:05,300 --> 00:48:07,740
Someone should remind him this is a hospital,

452
00:48:07,740 --> 00:48:09,620
so the patients should come first.

453
00:48:10,530 --> 00:48:11,490
Yes, Doctor.

454
00:48:12,770 --> 00:48:14,050
How could you like him?

455
00:48:14,750 --> 00:48:15,810
He’s so plain.

456
00:48:16,480 --> 00:48:17,570
You have terrible taste.

457
00:48:21,050 --> 00:48:22,020
What are you waiting for?

458
00:48:22,450 --> 00:48:23,440
Get back to work.

459
00:48:23,930 --> 00:48:24,760
Yes, Doctor.

460
00:48:24,760 --> 00:48:26,620
I’ll go check on the patients.

461
00:48:26,620 --> 00:48:27,520
You too.

462
00:49:01,580 --> 00:49:03,220
Who’s in charge of bed two?

463
00:49:04,760 --> 00:49:06,250
Uh, I am.

464
00:49:11,440 --> 00:49:12,220
Look at this.

465
00:49:15,570 --> 00:49:17,570
The wound contact layer is way too small.

466
00:49:17,800 --> 00:49:19,710
What if the gauze sticks to the patient’s wound?

467
00:49:22,080 --> 00:49:22,940
I’m sorry.

468
00:49:24,860 --> 00:49:25,800
Do it again.

469
00:49:28,180 --> 00:49:28,960
Yes.

470
00:49:29,970 --> 00:49:32,860
Could you take your job more seriously?

471
00:49:33,200 --> 00:49:34,960
Instead of fooling around like earlier.

472
00:49:37,490 --> 00:49:38,930
This is a hospital.

473
00:49:39,700 --> 00:49:41,480
The patients are the most important,

474
00:49:43,520 --> 00:49:44,750
not a male nurse.

475
00:49:49,180 --> 00:49:50,060
Yes.

476
00:50:09,800 --> 00:50:10,830
Yu.

477
00:50:12,330 --> 00:50:13,530
Yes?

478
00:50:14,100 --> 00:50:15,980
Dr. Reungrich asked me to get you.

479
00:50:16,650 --> 00:50:18,540
Oh, okay.

480
00:50:19,420 --> 00:50:21,060
He wants you there right now.

481
00:50:26,100 --> 00:50:26,930
Got it.

482
00:51:28,350 --> 00:51:31,080
"You think this is handsome?"

483
00:51:31,440 --> 00:51:32,580
Not really.

484
00:51:34,180 --> 00:51:35,330
You’re cute.

485
00:51:36,020 --> 00:51:37,080
"How could you like him?"

486
00:51:37,340 --> 00:51:39,110
The others just like you,

487
00:51:41,260 --> 00:51:42,400
but I love you.

488
00:51:43,740 --> 00:51:45,140
"He looks like a lizard."

489
00:51:47,810 --> 00:51:49,410
"He’s skinny as a grasshopper."

490
00:51:49,790 --> 00:51:53,460
I think this lean build is pretty cute.

491
00:51:54,420 --> 00:51:57,670
"The patients should come first."

492
00:52:00,820 --> 00:52:01,720
But right now…

493
00:52:02,690 --> 00:52:04,150
can your boyfriend come first?

494
00:52:05,390 --> 00:52:07,500
"This is a hospital."

495
00:52:08,070 --> 00:52:09,890
But this is our room.

496
00:52:10,840 --> 00:52:11,580
Hm?

497
00:52:12,520 --> 00:52:15,220
"How could you like someone so plain?"

498
00:52:15,680 --> 00:52:17,590
"You have terrible taste."

499
00:52:20,850 --> 00:52:22,700
"The wound contact layer is way too small."

500
00:52:23,350 --> 00:52:25,860
"What if the gauze sticks to the patient’s wound?"

501
00:52:26,540 --> 00:52:28,190
Actually, you did it correctly.

502
00:52:29,240 --> 00:52:31,870
It was just a little too small.

503
00:52:32,360 --> 00:52:33,490
Just a tiny bit.

504
00:52:45,790 --> 00:52:48,440
Did you really have to be that hard on me, Dr. Rich?

505
00:52:52,000 --> 00:52:53,480
No, I didn’t have to.

506
00:52:54,440 --> 00:52:55,410
I’m sorry.

507
00:52:56,240 --> 00:52:59,360
I didn’t know I was that harsh.

508
00:53:00,140 --> 00:53:03,070
I know you don’t want anyone to find out about us.

509
00:53:04,150 --> 00:53:05,590
But this is a bit too much.

510
00:53:06,580 --> 00:53:08,590
People will think you’re crazy.

511
00:53:15,120 --> 00:53:18,300
Is it really that big of a deal?

512
00:53:26,480 --> 00:53:27,590
Yeah, it’s this big.

513
00:53:39,250 --> 00:53:40,150
Do you want to?

514
00:53:41,710 --> 00:53:42,710
Are you hungry?

515
00:53:43,600 --> 00:53:44,710
I’m tired.

516
00:54:09,690 --> 00:54:11,390
No matter how tired, you still have to eat.

517
00:55:47,990 --> 00:55:49,400
Are you still mad at me?

518
00:55:51,010 --> 00:55:52,170
No.

519
00:55:53,280 --> 00:55:55,970
Next time, go a little easier on me.

520
00:55:59,320 --> 00:56:00,170
Yes, sir.
